# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and checked out as-is.
#
# Without this the repository held a mix: two specs were committed CRLF, one LF,
# the Python files CRLF, and `core.autocrlf` is false so nothing reconciled them.
# An editor that rewrote a file wholesale then produced a diff of the entire file
# — one edit came within a commit of landing 1,800 lines of churn for 61 lines of
# content, which is the kind of diff nobody reads and a real change can hide in.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `eol=native`: the working tree matches the repository, so
# what a reviewer reads is what is stored, and a tool that rewrites a file cannot
# flip its endings as a side effect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and cached payloads: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.gz binary
*.gct binary
*.npz binary
*.h5ad binary
*.zip binary
